        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> Closing as not planned.\r\n\r\n> [windwp/nvim-autopairs@`0f04d78`/lua/nvim-autopairs.lua#L173](https://github.com/windwp/nvim-autopairs/blob/0f04d78619cce9a5af4f355968040f7d675854a1/lua/nvim-autopairs.lua#L173)\r\n> \r\n> Thank you, found something in another repo.\r\n\r\n@echasnovski hello, I've tried with the approach linked by @konosubakonoakua and it works quite good, would you re-consider this feature?\r\n\r\nI tried with something as simple as:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/lua/mini/pairs.lua b/lua/mini/pairs.lua\r\nindex 2d109f8..740f524 100644\r\n--- a/lua/mini/pairs.lua\r\n+++ b/lua/mini/pairs.lua\r\n@@ -474,7 +474,7 @@ H.create_autocommands = function()\r\n   au('FileType', { 'TelescopePrompt', 'fzf' }, function() vim.b.minipairs_disable = true end, 'Disable locally')\r\n end\r\n\r\n-H.is_disabled = function() return vim.g.minipairs_disable == true or vim.b.minipairs_disable == true end\r\n+H.is_disabled = function() return vim.g.minipairs_disable == true or vim.b.minipairs_disable == true or (vim.fn.reg_recording() ~= '' or vim.fn.reg_executing() ~= '') end\r\n\r\n -- Pair registration ----------------------------------------------------------\r\n H.register_pair = function(pair_info, mode, buffer)\r\n```\r\n\r\nbut I guess it could be made more complete by adding a config flag (not sure if there's a lot of value on that but looks like nvim-autopairs has one 🤷🏼 )",
